I have everything needed. Here is my thorough report.

## Summary

This is the `spring-petclinic-rest` app running on the **OfficeFloor** REST framework (Maven build). The create-owner flow is defined declaratively in YAML that chains Java "function" classes. The request/response DTOs are **generated from OpenAPI** (they are `OwnerFieldsDto` / `OwnerDto`, not `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse`), so no hand-written DTO source files exist.

Note a load-bearing discrepancy I found (see end): the acceptance tests expect telephone **normalization** (strip non-digits, then require exactly 10), but no code currently normalizes.

---

## 1. OfficeFloor REST YAML for owners (create)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — the create pipeline:
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"
validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  next: build
build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save
save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond
respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```
So the chain is: **ValidateOwnerFields → BuildOwner → SaveOwner → RespondWithOwnerCreated**.

Related owner YAMLs (same directory `.../officefloor/rest/api/`):
- `owners.GET.yml` (references `ListOwners`)
- `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml`
- `owners/{ownerId}/pets.POST.yml`, `.../pets/{petId}.PUT/.GET.yml`, `.../pets/{petId}/visits.POST.yml`
- `v2/owners.GET.yml`

Escalation (400-handler) wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`:
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler
```

## 2. Java function classes referenced by the POST YAML

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`** — only checks presence/blankness of firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone. No format/normalization:
```java
public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
        throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
    require("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
    require("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
    require("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
    require("city", request.getCity(), missing);
    require("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
    if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
    }
    validated.set(request);
}
private static void require(String field, String value, List<String> missing) {
    if (value == null || value.isBlank()) { missing.add(field); }
}
```

**`.../owner/BuildOwner.java`** — maps DTO to entity via MapStruct:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
}
```

**`.../owner/SaveOwner.java`**:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

**`.../owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`**:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```

Supporting mapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct `@Mapper`; `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`, `toOwnerDto(Owner)`, plus page/collection mappings.

Escalation classes:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsException.java` — carries a `List<String> fields`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java` — responds `400` with body `{"errors": [...fieldNames]}`.

## 3. Owner entity + DTOs (telephone + validation)

**Entity `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** (extends `Person`). Telephone field with validation annotations:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
Also `@NotEmpty` on `address`, `city`. Superclass `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` has `@NotEmpty firstName`, `@NotEmpty lastName`.

**DTOs are generated, not source files.** They come from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` via the openapi-generator plugin into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` with suffix `Dto` (so `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPageDto`), emitted to `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` (not currently generated — no `target/` dir present). The schema (openapi.yml line 1991+):
```yaml
OwnerFields:                # -> OwnerFieldsDto (request body for POST /owners)
  properties:
    firstName: { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 30, pattern: "^[\p{L}]+([ '-][\p{L}]+){0,2}$" }
    lastName:  { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 30, pattern: "^[\p{L}]+([ '-][\p{L}]+){0,2}\.?$" }
    address:   { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 255 }
    city:      { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 80 }
    telephone:
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 20
      pattern: '^[0-9]*$'      # digits only, but NO fixed length
      example: '6085551023'
  required: [firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone]
Owner:                       # -> OwnerDto (response); allOf OwnerFields + readOnly id + pets[]
```
The POST operation (`operationId: addOwner`, openapi.yml line 65) takes `OwnerFields`, returns `201` with `Owner`, `400`/`500` with `ProblemDetail`.

Note the **two telephone rules diverge**: the generated DTO pattern is `^[0-9]*$` (any length, digits only), while the JPA entity `Owner` requires exactly `^[0-9]{10}$`.

`ApplyOwner.java` (used by the PUT/update flow, not POST) also copies telephone: `owner.setTelephone(request.getTelephone())`.

## 4. Tests for creating owners / telephone

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

**`AcceptanceTest.java`** — the telephone-focused checkpoint. Class Javadoc: *"telephone-normalize: On create, normalize the telephone by removing every non-digit character, then require exactly [10 digits]"*:
```java
@Test void coreStripsToTenDigits() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "(04) 1234-5678");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("0412345678"));
}
@Test void errorRejectsTooFewDigits() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "12345");
    createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
}
```

**`AcceptanceBase.java`** — `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={OWNER_ADMIN,VET_ADMIN,ADMIN})`. Drives everything through `POST /api/owners` and reads back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` using `MockMvc`. Key helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully-valid unique payload), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`/`createOwnerWithKey`, `getOwner`/`fetchOwner`, `extractId` (from `id` field or `Location` header), `uniqueTelephone()` = `04` + 8 digits (10 total). Also pinned lookup tables and Luhn/SHA helpers for other rules.

**`AuditLogCapture.java`** — test utility capturing the `AUDIT` Logback logger for asserting audit side-effects.

## 5. Build system / running tests

Maven, single module `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (`artifactId: spring-petclinic-rest`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`). Tests run via the standard Surefire lifecycle (no custom surefire/failsafe config; parent defaults apply):
- `./mvnw test` (or `mvn test`) — runs the JUnit 5 acceptance tests.
- `./mvnw verify` / `package` — full build.

Relevant build wiring:
- **openapi-generator-maven-plugin** 7.23.0 (`generate` goal): input `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, `generatorName=spring`, `interfaceOnly=true`, `performBeanValidation=true`, `modelNameSuffix=Dto`, models → `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, APIs → `...rest.api`.
- **build-helper-maven-plugin** adds `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` as a source root.
- **maven-compiler-plugin** with MapStruct 1.6.3 annotation processor (`defaultComponentModel=spring`).
- Test deps: `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test`, `mockito-core`, OfficeFloor `woof_test`, `json-path`. Jacoco coverage `check` + `report` bound.

## Key finding (load-bearing gap)

The acceptance tests require telephone **normalization on create** (`"(04) 1234-5678"` → stored/returned as `"0412345678"`; `"12345"` → 400). Currently:
- `ValidateOwnerFields` only checks blank/missing — it does **not** strip non-digits or enforce a digit count.
- The generated `OwnerFieldsDto` pattern `^[0-9]*$` would already **reject** `"(04) 1234-5678"` (non-digits) rather than normalize it, and would **accept** `"12345"`.
- The `Owner` entity's `^[0-9]{10}$` requires exactly 10 digits but there is no code path that transforms input before validation.

No component in the POST chain performs the "strip non-digits then require exactly 10" behavior the tests expect, so both `AcceptanceTest` cases would currently fail as written.

